  <front>
    <title abbrev="deflate out">Raw DEFLATE written into a caller's buffer</title>
    <seriesInfo name="Internet-Draft" value="draft-deflate-out-00"/>
    <author initials="V." surname="Fixture" fullname="Vector Fixture">
      <organization>vector</organization>
      <address>
      </address>
    </author>
    <date year="2026" month="November" day="19"/>
    <abstract>
      <?line 13?>

<t>A fixture, not a specification: raw DEFLATE as nish's std compress writes
it, into a caller's buffer from an index, answering the index just past the
last byte or a negative code. The interface declares each (out, at) -&gt; end
write as a bytes result, and the negative code as null.</t>
    </abstract>
  </front>
  <middle>
    <?line 20?>

<section anchor="introduction">
      <name>Introduction</name>
      <t>The key words "<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>", "<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>", "<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHALL
NOT</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>", "<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>", "<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>", "<bcp14>NOT RECOMMENDED</bcp14>",
"<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>", and "<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>" in this document are to be interpreted as
described in BCP 14 <xref target="RFC2119"/> <xref target="RFC8174"/> when, and only when, they
appear in all capitals, as shown here.</t>
      <?line -18?>

<t>The module is nish's own nish/compress/deflate, checked and run with
<tt>--nish-root</tt>. Its tests in tests/spec/emit run the same emitted test
against copies of it that write past the end they answer, which the contract
refuses. A compressor's output is not fixed, so the compressed vector is a
stored block, which zlib and nish write alike, and a property checks the
rest by a round trip.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="interface">
      <name>Interface</name>
      <sourcecode type="ts-interface"><![CDATA[
// module: nish/compress/deflate
export const deflateCompress = (src: u8[] /* window */, out: u8[] /* out 2 * src.length + 18 */, level: i32): u8[]
export const deflateDecompress = (src: u8[] /* window */, out: u8[] /* out 4096 */, limit: i32): u8[] | null
]]></sourcecode>
    </section>
    <section anchor="compress">
      <name>Compressing</name>
      <t anchor="R-DEFLATE-STORED">deflateCompress <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> write a raw DEFLATE stream of the window's bytes, and
at level 0 that stream <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> be stored blocks.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="decompress">
      <name>Decompressing</name>
      <t anchor="R-INFLATE">deflateDecompress <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> write the bytes a raw DEFLATE stream holds, and only
those bytes.</t>
      <t anchor="R-INFLATE-TRUNCATED">deflateDecompress <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> return null for a stream that ends before its last
block does.</t>
      <sourcecode type="ts-property"><![CDATA[
// P-ROUND-TRIP covers R-INFLATE — what deflateCompress writes, deflateDecompress reads back
forall (d: u8[] /* 0..64 */) => {
  const e = deflateDecompress(deflateCompress(d, 6), 4096);
  return e !== null && unwrap(e) === d;
}
]]></sourcecode>
    </section>
    <section anchor="arguments">
      <name>Arguments</name>
      <t>The vectors compress at Level = 0, which stores the bytes, and decompress
with Limit = 4096, the capacity the interface declares.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations">
      <name>Security Considerations</name>
      <t>A stream can claim far more output than its length: <tt>limit</tt> and the
capacity bound what deflateDecompress writes.</t>
    </section>
